---
title:    "Set Functions for Functional Logic Programming"
citation: "(PPDP 2009)"
url:      "https://www.michaelhanus.de/papers/PPDP09.html"
date:     2009-01-01 # used for sorting, most recent first, should usually match the papers date
---
This paper proposes set functions as a new feature
to encapsulate nondeterministic computations in Curry.
In contrast to previous approaches,
the result of set functions is independent of their evaluation order.
Thus, they can be considered as a declarative approach to encapsulate search.